<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico completes secondary intervention.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico completes secondary intervention.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico assigned all three direct sales of paper and six repurchase agreements whereby it had sought to drain 4.287 billion pesos from the secondary market on Thursday, dealers said.</p>
<p>The Cetes sales were assigned as follows:</p>
<p>    AMOUNT     TERM	 AVERAGE RATE</p>
<p>    150 million    364 days   20.97 pct</p>
<p>    150 million    181 days   20.53 pct</p>
<p>    150 million     91 days   19.45 pct</p>
<p>The terms and maturities of the repurchase agreements were placed as follows:</p>
<p>    600 million     64 days   20.46 pct</p>
<p>    700 million     49 days   20.15 pct</p>
<p>    750 million     43 days   20.23 pct</p>
<p>    750 million     21 days   20.24 pct</p>
<p>    850 million     19 days   20.54 pct</p>
<p>    187 million	1 day    19.98 pct</p>
<p>*Amounts in pesos</p>
<p>(( --Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
